version: "2.0"
name: gnomon-kernel-git
description: >-
  Kernel git verbs: the git operations the kernel runs for sessions and loops
  (verbs.ts, kernel-verbs.ts, verb-exec.ts), the scratch worktrees loops work in
  (scratch.ts) and landing their result (land.ts).
context:
  - >-
    The ^git-init-gate and ^git-push-gate gates stay in
    packages/gnomon/.purpose.
  - >-
    Split out of packages/gnomon/.purpose (2026-10-27); path: values stay
    relative to packages/gnomon, the package root.
components:
  git-verbs:
    description: >-
      #git-verbs (T-2026-10-23-002; spec §6.6). The kernel runs git for a
      session OUTSIDE its sandbox, because the session profile denies writes
      to .git/config, .git/hooks and .git/info (a config or hook the agent
      wrote would run unsandboxed under the human's own git) and has no
      credential access. Verbs: git.init, git.push, repo.create (gh),
      git.worktree.add, git.worktree.remove — reached through #kernel-mcp
      (gnomon_git_init, gnomon_git_push, gnomon_repo_create,
      gnomon_worktree_add, gnomon_worktree_remove). src/kernel/git/verbs.ts
      (pure): initConfigText (the [core] template only: nothing executable,
      branch main), initRefusal (a session root; not home, a system folder or
      the Gnomon home; not already in a repo, an ancestor's .git included),
      dotGitOf (lstat only: a symlinked .git or a gitfile pointer is never
      followed; a remnant .git a failed sandboxed init left is cleared),
      configProblems (push/create/worktree run only on a repo config of plain
      keys, CONFIG_ALLOW; hooksPath, fsmonitor, sshCommand, credential.*,
      include*, filter.*, url.*.insteadOf, receivepack… refuse
      unsafe-config), parseRemote (https or ssh to a plain host only; ext::,
      file, git://, http, local paths, userinfo, query refuse bad-remote),
      hostWarning (punycode, non-ASCII, near misses of forge hosts: the card
      is flagged claim-mismatch and offers no Always), argument validators
      (no leading '-', no '..', no control characters; '--' before every
      operand), the card composers. verb-exec.ts: async spawn (argv, no
      shell, capped output, SIGKILL at the timeout); init uses the hardened
      env (no global/system config: the human's templateDir or hooksPath
      never reach the repo); push and gh use a SCRUBBED env (HOME = the
      user's, so their credential helper and gh sign-in apply; never
      GH_TOKEN, GIT_DIR, proxies, askpass or GIT_SSH_COMMAND from the daemon)
      and PUSH_GIT_FLAGS (no hooks, no fsmonitor, protocols https/ssh only,
      no redirects, no submodules, no follow-tags, GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL);
      redactOutput (URL userinfo and token shapes). kernel-verbs.ts GitVerbs:
      every call writes git.verb{phase:'requested'} first, then refused{why},
      ran or failed{why, exitCode}; rows carry ids, closed values and the
      kernel-resolved host only (never a URL, path, token or output). One
      verb at a time per root. Kernel worktrees live at
      <root>/.gnomon/worktrees/<name> (made with hooks off, excluded from the
      main checkout's status); the session profile's kernelWorktrees denies
      (manifest/policy.ts worktree-guard / worktree-gitdir + steering under
      W) keep their steering, .git pointer, .mcp.json and git-dir pointers
      kernel-only, and the supervisor judges an edit there against the
      worktree as its root (#editRoots). Claude Code's own worktree
      isolation (.claude/worktrees) and `git worktree add` stay refused by
      the sandbox (measured); the session guidance names the verbs.
      Darwin-first (win32: parity phase; no verb is served on win32).
      Aegis review 2026-10-23: push/create run under a kernel config
      snapshot (credential.* + core.sshCommand only, ssh -F a copied
      ~/.ssh/config; GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM, GIT_COMMON_DIR pinned); each root's
      .git, commondir, remotes/ and branches/ are session-denied; legacy
      remotes refuse; a worktree base with different steering files forces
      the card (M1); gh only from fixed trusted locations (M4); pushed
      commits are secret-scanned and a hit always takes a card (M5); an
      explicit force-with-lease sha (L3); at most four verb calls in flight
      per session (L5); gh api user is a `lookup` row (L6). Session file
      writes are deny-by-default (T-2026-10-23-004, policy.writeAllow,
      probe p10m-write-allow, test/write-allow-sandbox.test.ts).
      GitVerbs.close() (daemon shutdown, $daemon-lifecycle): no snapshot
      capture starts after it, and every capture in flight (the daemon's
      fire-and-forget start-up refreshPushConfig spawns git several times and
      writes <home>/git-verbs/{gitconfig.<pid>.<ms>, ssh_config, gitconfig})
      settles before shutdown releases the daemon lock, so no write lands in
      the home after shutdown resolves (it raced a successor kernel and the
      tests' rmSync of the home: ENOTEMPTY in afterEach, leaked temp homes).
    path: src/kernel/git/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, kernel, git, security, paradigm-8]
    signals: []
    tests:
      - test/git-verbs.test.ts
      - test/git-verbs-sandbox.test.ts
      - test/write-allow-sandbox.test.ts
      - test/daemon-lifecycle.test.ts
    oracles: [G-GIT-04, G-GIT-05, G-GIT-06, G-GIT-07]
  loop-git:
    description: >-
      #loop-git (docs/specs/gnomon-loops.md §3.2 where loops work, §3.3 kill
      switch, §4 retention; build plan step 10, LP6a; G-GIT-01).
      src/kernel/git/scratch.ts. The scratch worktree for a run with act
      nodes is the HEAD tree, detached, written into the KERNEL-OWNED run dir
      <home>/loop-work/act-<runId>/tree (0700, never inside the repo, no .git)
      from hardened git plumbing only (rev-parse, ls-tree -r -z -l, cat-file
      --batch: raw blobs, no filters, no textconv, no checkout, no hook;
      HARDENED_GIT_FLAGS --no-optional-locks, core.hooksPath=/dev/null,
      core.fsmonitor=false, core.sshCommand=false, protocol.allow=never,
      credential.helper empty; hardenedGitEnv: a clean env with no inherited
      GIT_*, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM, GIT_ATTR_NOSYSTEM).
      Not `git worktree add`: that writes the human's .git and runs a checkout
      with the repo's filters and hooks. Files O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW,
      links last, node_modules linked only when their realpath is inside the
      repo; caps 50 000 files and 500 MiB. liveScratch(runId) is the module
      table LocalLane.openLoop checks (a forged path is never a scratch).
      scratchChanges diffs in-kernel by git blob id against the HEAD
      manifest. parkScratch writes the changed blobs (hash-object -w
      --no-filters), a tree through a private GIT_INDEX_FILE and a commit
      (Gnomon Loop <loop+<id>@gnomon.invalid>, trailers Gnomon-Loop and
      Gnomon-Run after the stripped message) into a kernel-owned bare park
      repo <home>/loop-work/park/<repoHash>.git whose objects borrow the
      human's through alternates, at refs/gnomon/loops/<id>/<runId>; the
      human repo gets no ref and no object until #loop-land moves them in
      under the land lock (src/kernel/git/land.ts). diff-tree -p
      --no-renames --no-ext-diff --no-textconv for the card. removeScratch at
      run end; sweepLoopScratch (boot, LOOP_RETENTION_DAYS) removes stale run
      dirs and parked refs past the window, never a live scratch. Aegis
      review: case- and NFD-colliding trees refused, parents created one
      component at a time and realpath-checked before every write or link;
      reads O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK with fstat (regular, nlink 1, capped), FIFOs
      refused, park re-checks each blob against the scanned oid (PARK_LIMITS);
      git resolved once to an absolute path, at least 2.39.4,
      GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=none, GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES, the uid check in place
      of safe.directory, no gpg signing; names with control, format or bidi
      characters refused. Residual: hash-object through alternates freshens
      the mtime of an object the human store already has.
    path: src/kernel/git/scratch.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, loops, git, paradigm-8, security]
    tests:
      - test/loop-act-e2e.test.ts
      - test/loop-act.test.ts
    anchors:
      - src/kernel/git/scratch.ts
      - src/kernel/git/index.ts
